KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ both A subobjects destroyed: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The program is rejected: "function E::~E(): conversion between 'struct D
&' and 'struct A &' through the ambiguous base class 'A'"
(cpp_typecheck_compound_type.cpp).  E's implicit destructor converts to
the repeated base A, which [class.mi]/3 makes ambiguous; it should only
call D's destructor.  With V a non-virtual base the conversion to V fails
the same way; without virtual functions the program verifies.  D itself,
as a complete object, works.  Found while testing construction vtables;
the W188 build rejects it as well.
